  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "S2 was the decisive battleground: the final text keeps a 5% limit but removes any sales stop for over-limit models, so Hearth 10 can keep being sold during corrective action, while customers still receive per-model results and the public sees only aggregated data. S5 mandates a recall at the 8/100k trigger with no transition, which captures Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9), while S3 and S4 use the 6-year retrofit and 36-month suppression lead time that fit both companies' red lines. The S1 reporting regime is the strongest section for public safety."
